  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">Scope: every message sent or consumed here. Job Contract envelopes with deterministic `idempotencyKey` (`IntakeEngine:{runId}:{operation}:{dispatchAttempt}`, as built by task 001 — one run sends `segment` then `redline` under the same dispatch attempt, so the key carries the operation; following the colon convention of `Communication:{messageId}:Process` and `DocAnalysis:{documentId}`), ids and blob paths only; the completion and timeout handlers implement `IJobHandler` and claim atomically, so a duplicate completion or a completion after timeout changes nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Scope: logs, exceptions and messages. Run id, blob path ids, outcome codes and durations only; no document bytes, plan content or clause text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: blob and Service Bus access. Managed identity only via the existing BlobGateway and ServiceBusClient registrations; no SAS, keys or connection strings.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-052">Scope: timeout enforcement and the completion consumer. The timeout is a scheduled Service Bus message handled by an `IJobHandler`; no timer `BackgroundService`, no polling loop. The one hosted service added is `IntakeEngineCompletionProcessor`, a Service Bus queue consumer copied from `CommunicationJobProcessor` (same `ServiceBusClient`, same retry and dead-letter reason codes); it is registered only when `ServiceBus:IntakeEngineCompletionQueueName` is non-empty (default empty: the queue exists only on stamps with `deployIntakeEngine=true`), so no stamp starts a consumer for a missing queue.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: the completion handler. A completion is UNTRUSTED input (it comes from the container that parses untrusted documents). Accept only `runId`, `dispatchAttempt`, the outcome code and the check outcome from the message. The run must exist, be awaiting the engine, and its current dispatch attempt must equal the message's; otherwise log ids only and complete with no change. Never read or copy a blob path taken from the message: derive the output paths from `runId` with the 001 path contract, inside the staging container.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the orchestrator. Do not edit `Services/Intake/IntakeRunJobHandler.cs`; the completion handler resumes the run by enqueuing an `IntakeRun` continuation Job Contract (deterministic key) so 013's resume rules apply unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-005">Scope: staging layout. Flat, deterministic paths under the staging container keyed by run id; outputs are copied into SPE by the harness (015), never served from staging.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Scope: the PR. State the Placement Justification, measure the publish-size delta against a fresh master build, ≤ 60 MB total, no new package and no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

