  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Agree the envelope fields and path convention from task 001's envelope.py; write them as constants in the dispatcher.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement IntakeEngineDispatcher: stage source and plan with `CreateIfNotExistsAsync` at `{runId}/in/…`; record engine execution id / staging prefix on the run (task 011 columns); send the request envelope; schedule an `IntakeEngineTimeout` message at now + timeout. The timeout must exceed the engine job's own retry window (task 001: delays 1+2+4+8 min across deliveries 1–4, plus run time), or set it from `JobContract.RetryDelay`; a 10-minute timeout fails runs the engine is still retrying.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the engine-queue send and scheduled-enqueue methods to JobSubmissionService.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement IntakeEngineCompletionJobHandler: claim, verify run is awaiting engine, record outputs' paths and check-report outcome, hand back to the orchestrator by enqueuing an `IntakeRun` continuation Job Contract; `check_outputs` failure → held with admin attention.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement IntakeEngineTimeoutJobHandler: if the run is still awaiting the engine, mark it Failed with reason "engine timeout" (terminal last); otherwise no-op.</step>
    <step order="6">Register in JobProcessingModule; write tests (dispatch payload is ids-only; duplicate completion no-op; completion after timeout no-op; timeout fails only a waiting run; check failure holds); run an integration round trip against Azurite or dev staging if available.</step>
    <step order="7">`dotnet build`, `dotnet test`; measure publish size vs fresh master.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations in `projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the completion processor cannot follow `CommunicationJobProcessor` as written (it needs a second `ServiceBusClient`, a new package, or changes to `ServiceBusJobProcessor`), STOP and escalate (ADR-052 / root CLAUDE.md §17).</trigger>
    <trigger>If task 001's envelope or path contract differs from what this task needs, STOP and reconcile with the 001 owner; do not fork the contract.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>reuse-scan.md row 6 (claim-check staging): `Infrastructure/Storage/BlobGateway.cs:148`, verdict "extend/use BlobGateway"; CAPABILITY-INDEX row 6 (queue work: `JobSubmissionService`, `IJobHandler`). No existing BFF code talks to an out-of-process engine.</existing>
    <extension>Partly — BlobGateway and JobSubmissionService are reused/extended (one send method); the dispatcher and two handlers are new because no existing handler waits on an external consumer's completion. The completion processor copies `CommunicationJobProcessor`; `ServiceBusJobProcessor` cannot be reused because it serves `sdap-jobs`, which the engine identity must not be able to send to.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The NDA harness cannot hand the document and plan to the engine or learn the result, and a hung engine leaves a run waiting forever (FR-09, NFR-05 fail). Without the dedicated completion queue the engine identity needs Sender on `sdap-jobs`, and a parser exploit could enqueue any BFF job.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

