  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a run at Build, dispatch stages inputs at deterministic paths and sends one envelope whose payload contains only ids/paths; a repeat dispatch for the same run sends no second request (staging writes are create-if-not-exists).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a valid completion, the run records the output paths and check outcome and advances; a duplicate completion changes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a completion reporting a `check_outputs` failure holds the run with admin attention and nothing is sent for approval (FR-09c).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with no completion within the timeout, the run is marked Failed with reason "engine timeout"; a completion arriving after that is a no-op (NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">correlationId is identical on the run, the request envelope, the completion handling logs and the timeout message (NFR-06); no captured log or message contains document content (NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a message on the completion queue with any `JobType` other than `IntakeEngineCompleted` is dead-lettered `WrongQueue` and no handler runs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a completion naming an unknown run, a run not awaiting the engine, or a stale `dispatchAttempt` changes nothing (ids-only log, message completed); a blob path in the message is ignored and the handler reads only the paths it derives from `runId`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The only hosted service added is `IntakeEngineCompletionProcessor` (no timer or polling loop); with `ServiceBus:IntakeEngineCompletionQueueName` empty it is not registered; DiGraphValidationTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PR states Placement Justification and publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes. All tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Completion path revised 2026-11-25 (owner): dedicated engine identity + own completion queue + dedicated BFF processor; see notes/decisions.md. Effort xhigh: multi-file concurrency/race work (completion vs timeout) with a complete spec. Seeding proof requested for the late-completion-after-timeout guard (a regression would resurrect a failed run): remove the state check, confirm the test fails, restore. Deterministic anchoring (owner 2026-11-26, notes/decisions.md): segment_clauses runs first (engine job `segment` operation); the edit-plan AI picks `para` only from the closed para_key list and quotes verbatim; the BFF exact-match pre-check refuses bad anchors (closed codes) before the engine; never fuzzy, approximate or whole-document text matching. Dispatch carries an operation field (segment | redline); the BFF reads clauses.json from staging by a path it derives from runId/attempt, never from the completion. Task 001 (2026-11-26) completion envelope carries `operation` (`segment`|`redline`), the outcome, and for `plan_does_not_fit` the edit index and closed reason code (codes only, never engine stderr); the consumer must handle both operations. The engine contract is in notes/001-engine-container.md and notes/009-engine-changes.md. Application Insights is a fourth outbound host for the job (task 002 telemetry setting), beyond the three in task 001 criterion 11. Update 2026-11-26 (task 001 commit 3964def44d, skip mode on by default): `completed` may carry non-empty `refusedEdits` (0-based `edit` + closed code) and `refusedBookmarks`, meaning success with by-hand edits; a codes-only blob `{runId}/out/redline/{dispatchAttempt}/refused-report.json` is written; `plan_does_not_fit` with empty lists = plan broke the engine contract; `contract_error` (dead-lettered Poisoned) covers malformed engine stderr or unknown codes. The refused count and by-hand list feed the approval Work Item (task 015).</notes>

